  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 176000,
    "kind": "switching fabric",
    "note": "176 Gbps switching capacity (256 Gbps with StackWise-80 stacking), 130.95 Mpps forwarding (190 Mpps stacked) - data sheet Table 9. mGig downlinks counted at 10G in that total."
  },
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/collateral/switches/catalyst-9200-series-switches/nb-06-cat9200-ser-data-sheet-cte-en.html",
  "notes": [
    "Port census and PoE totals: Cisco Catalyst 9200 Series data sheet, Table 1 and Table 4 (https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/collateral/switches/catalyst-9200-series-switches/nb-06-cat9200-ser-data-sheet-cte-en.html); per-model port layout and StackWise-80 in the Catalyst 9200 hardware installation guide, Table 1 (https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst9200/hardware/install/b-c9200-hig/product_overview.html).",
    "Stacking: StackWise-80, 80 Gbps, up to 8 C9200L members and \"up to 384 access ports\" per stack, C9200L-STACK-KIT; fixed C9200L cannot stack with modular C9200 or other Catalyst switches (data sheet Table 5).",
    "Console and management: RJ-45 console (EIA/TIA-232) plus USB mini-Type B console, one 10/100/1000BASE-T RJ-45 Ethernet management port and USB Type A storage ports on the front panel (hardware installation guide, \"Management Ports\").",
    "Software: Cisco IOS XE Release 16.9.2 or later (data sheet). Fixed power supplies, fixed redundant fans, no network-module slot on C9200L.",
    "Uplink wording: the data sheet says \"4x 1/10G fixed uplinks\", the installation guide says \"4x10G SFP+ fixed uplink ports\". The cages are declared as accepting both 1G and 10G, following the data sheet."
  ]
